    <Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:comment"/>
        <Literal>Last Updated: 2023/06/11</Literal>
    </Annotation>
    <Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="owl:versionInfo"/>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal">3.1</Literal>
    </Annotation>
    <Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.org/dc/terms/description"/>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">To codify the principles from the PORTAL-DOORS Project and NPDS Cyberinfrastructure, an ontology named PDP-DREAM has been created for the  DREAM principles in order to consolidate the entire collection of principles (those for software architecture, experimental science, and social engineering) into a formal specification. This PDP-DREAM ontology has been developed in OWL 2.0. The current version of this ontology has four main sections corresponding to the DREAM principles, the HDMM architectural style, the NPDS cyberinfrastructure, and the FAIR metrics.</Literal>
    </Annotation>
    <Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified"/>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">v2.1 - Updated the ontology with a number of supporting foundational ontologies and have begun integration for FAIR metrics experiment

v1.4 - Further split NPDS-DREAM ontology into five-parts: FAIR, NPDS, HDMM, DREAM, and PDP-DREAM. Created PDP-DREAM core file.
v1.3 - Split NPDS-DREAM ontology into three subsections: FAIR, DREAM, and NPDS.
v1.2 - Merged the NPDS-DREAM and FAIR ontology into a single ontology, added elements beyond class hierarchy such as object properties.
v1.1 - Original creation of two-part PDP-DREAM ontology consisting of NPDS-DREAM and FAIR ontologies.</Literal>
    </Annotation>
    <Annotation>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://purl.org/dc/terms/title"/>
        <Literal>PDP-DREAM</Literal>
    </Annotation>
